# Dashboard environment. Copy to .env.local for local dev; on Vercel set the same names under
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables (then redeploy: NEXT_PUBLIC_* are fixed at build time).
#
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is embedded in the JavaScript bundle that ships to the browser.
# Anyone who opens the dashboard can read it. Never put a secret here.

# Base URL of the read-only run API (the root docker-compose `api` service, usually behind the
# Cloudflare tunnel). Must include the scheme. On Vercel (https) it must be https, or the browser
# blocks it as mixed content. No trailing path; a trailing slash is ignored.
# Leave empty (or unset) to run the dashboard on the bundled simulated sample:
# every view then says "REPLAY · SAMPLE DATA".
# Examples: https://posttrain-api.example.com   https://random-words.trycloudflare.com
#           http://127.0.0.1:8787  (local dev against `docker compose up`)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Read token for the API: must equal READ_TOKEN in the root .env used by docker compose.
# It is public by construction (it ships in the bundle). It only gates a read-only, redacted event
# stream. Use a long random value, not a password used anywhere else, and rotate it by changing
# READ_TOKEN and this variable together (then redeploy).
NEXT_PUBLIC_READ_TOKEN=
